  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market Development Facility - Phase 2 in Fiji</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market Development Facility (MDF) in Fiji aims to create additional employment and income opportunities for poor women and men through sustainable and broad-based pro-poor growth. Key sectors include tourism; high value agriculture; and urban industries. MDF analyses market dynamics and socio-economics to identify industries and sectors that can provide benefits for the poor, as customers, consumers, owners or employees of targeted small enterprise. MDF reduces the risks and costs of pre-commercial or early-stage opportunities and supports innovation through a blend of financial and non-financial support including: co-investment to help de-risk innovation and test new products, services and business models; market analysis to understand consumer and business trends; technical advice to develop new products/services and business models; and marketing and promotion.</narrative>
  </description>
